Manufacturing — The Open University (@mat-ou-manufacturing: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mat-sources) { r_5WVG0HEJ30KYA0GMVCHEZBY9X0
[Complete OpenLearn course](https://www.open.edu/openlearn/mod/oucontent/view.php?id=3226). Read all seven sections and their activities: product definition, casting, forming, cutting, joining, process economics and surface engineering. A gearwheel provides a concrete beginner's example; the course is listed as twenty introductory study hours and offers offline formats through its own download links.

The contents, introduction, powder-processing section 3.10 and physical-vapour-deposition section 7.5 were inspected on 30 October 2026. Treat the compressed taxonomy as an introduction: not every powder route includes die compaction, and sintering does not guarantee a homogeneous, pore-free solid. Compare these simplifications with the ceramic and metallurgy sources.

Authorized free institutional reading and downloads; a blanket adaptation licence for every included component was not established in this inspection. Preserve attribution and component permissions; link the course rather than copying its text or media into the repository.

**Return:** [Materials-engineering sources — reading and primary evidence](../Sources.lingua#r_51JAH6DB4WV2HZAB69G21ZHSMK).
